# ERP interface design standard

Apply this style to all future UI designs and requested interface changes in this project, unless the user explicitly requests another style. Apply it within the requested scope; do not redesign unrelated screens.

- Use the latest workshop interface as the reference: `src/components/WorkshopManagement.tsx` and `src/components/WorkshopManagementFields.tsx`.
- Use a restrained professional ERP layout with clear hierarchy, consistent spacing, meaningful statistics, and semantic theme colors. Preserve Arabic RTL, IQD, responsive behavior, and dark mode.
- Separate form titles, labels, and controls visibly. Prefer vertical field groups (`flex flex-col gap-3 leading-6`) and generous section spacing; dialogs must scroll on small screens without overlapping fields or clipping actions.
- Show full names and identifiers, especially the CTR code together with the project name. Use searchable pickers and wrapping text for long options and selected values.
- Present large staff lists in dedicated searchable, filterable views with attendance and actual cost-center context. Use bounded scrolling and progressive display/pagination where appropriate.
- Keep cards, tables, and controls consistent with existing Shadcn components. Provide clear loading, error, and empty states.
- When drag-and-drop ordering is relevant, persist it and provide accessible button/keyboard alternatives.
- Reuse these patterns according to the workflow; do not force every screen into identical cards or add unrelated functionality.
